 "name": "shelf-assembly",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "An assembly animation: a shelf unit putting itself together",
 "summary": "A small shelf unit of eleven boxes and cylinders assembling itself with Scene3D: the base, the sides, the back panel, two shelves, the top and the feet fly in from their own directions one step after another, hold, come apart and start again; drag to turn it at any time.",
 "prompt": "Animate how our small shelf unit goes together: the base first, then the sides, the back, the shelves, the top and the feet, each flying into place; let me turn it while it builds.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "CMP",
 "components": [
  "Scene3D"
 ],
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "3d.scene",
   "time.animation"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "3d.mesh",
   "input.drag"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "onboarding"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "3d",
  "assembly",
  "assembly animation",
  "assembly instructions",
  "exploded view",
  "explode",
  "build steps",
  "how it goes together",
  "furniture",
  "flat pack",
  "shelf",
  "bookcase",
  "parts fly in",
  "3d animation",
  "orbit"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "assemble: true flies each part in from its \"from\" offset (dx, dy, dz from its place), one step after another; parts with the same \"step\" move together (the two sides, the four feet)",
  "stagger sets the seconds between steps, hold how long the finished unit stays before it comes apart; the cycle repeats from continuousSec(), eased with smooth_step",
  "frame (auto: all with assemble) keeps the parts in view at their start offsets too: keep offsets near the object's own size or the finished unit gets small",
  "Mono shows the unit assembled and still, as hidden-line wireframes"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players only. Don't use it for a screen that must play on Android today",
  "The animation repaints every frame while the page is shown (it loops); offsets far larger than the object shrink the assembled view, because every offset stays framed"
 ],
